  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 213 PM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe potential MCS across east central and southeast NM Friday \nevening looks to result in a leftover MCV over southeast NM Saturday \nmorning with the 599 to 600 dam 500 mb high centered somewhere over \nthe Four Corners area. This MCV combined with PWATS around 1.1 to \n1.5 inches will result in an enhancement in shower and thunderstorm \ncoverage across central and western NM Saturday afternoon. This will \nincrease the risk for flash flooding especially across the Ruidoso \narea burn scars, and much of western NM from Gallup down to the Gila \nMountains. Morning cloud cover from the MCV could be a limiting \nfactor to thunderstorm development in the Ruidoso area, so this will \nbe something worth watching. The MCV moves into eastern AZ Sunday \nkeeping a higher coverage of thunderstorms across western and north \ncentral NM Sunday afternoon and evening. Central and eastern NM will \ncontinue seeing hot temperatures with highs in the mid 90s to around \n100 due to being under the 597 to 598 dam 500 mb high centered over \nsouthern CO and northern NM.\n\nNext work week looks to hot with 90s to mid 100s across central and \neastern NM and diurnal shower and thunderstorm coverage favoring \nwestern and north central areas due to recycled moisture (PWATS\naround 1 inch) rotating around the 595 to 598 dam upper high \ncentered over northeast NM and the TX and OK Panhandles through \nWednesday before pivoting west to over the heart of the Land of \nEnchantment next Thursday. &&",
